<title>NORWAY: Kvaerner wins NOK 295 mln sewage deal.</title>
<headline>Kvaerner wins NOK 295 mln sewage deal.</headline>
<dateline>OSLO 1997-04-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Construction and engineering group Kvaerner ASA said on Monday its Kvaerner Water division had won a contract worth 295 million crowns to build a new sewage works in west London for Thames Water.</p>
<p>Kvaerner Water is part of Kvaerner Construction Ltd.  </p>
<p>Kvaerner said the project would begin immediately and the plant was due to be in operation by the end of 1998.</p>
<p>The company has nearly finished construction of a large new pumping facility for Thames Water at Abbey Hills in east London.</p>
<p>--Oslo newsroom, +47 22 42 50 41</p>
